</table>

<h3 id="earthquake-magnitude">Earthquake / Magnitude</h3>
<p><strong>Definition:</strong> Earthquake = sudden release of energy from rock movement, causing shaking. Magnitude = the size, on a logarithmic scale (M6 vs M7 = 10× bigger).</p>
<p><strong>Visual cue:</strong> Seismogram showing shaking; magnitude scale showing log relationship.</p>
<p><strong>In a sentence:</strong> "The M9.1 Tōhoku earthquake released ~32× more energy than an M8."</p>
