</table>

<h3 id="liquefaction">Liquefaction</h3>
<p><strong>Definition:</strong> Saturated soil behaves like a liquid when shaken violently, causing buildings to sink, tilt, or float.</p>
<p><strong>Visual cue:</strong> Soil grains: orderly before shaking; suspended in water during shaking.</p>
<p><strong>In a sentence:</strong> "Anchorage 1964 liquefaction caused entire neighborhoods to flow downhill into Cook Inlet."</p>
