</table>

<h3 id="lithosphere-mantle">Lithosphere / Mantle</h3>
<p><strong>Definition:</strong> Lithosphere = Earth's rigid outer shell (~100 km thick); contains tectonic plates. Mantle = layer below, of slowly-flowing rock that drives plate motion.</p>
<p><strong>Visual cue:</strong> Cross-section of Earth showing crust + lithosphere + mantle.</p>
<p><strong>In a sentence:</strong> "Plate motion is driven by convection in the mantle below the lithosphere."</p>
