</table>

<h3 id="water-cycle">Water cycle</h3>
<p><strong>Definition:</strong> Continuous movement of water through evaporation, condensation, precipitation, runoff, infiltration. Earth's water doesn't disappear: it moves.</p>
<p><strong>Visual cue:</strong> Classic water cycle diagram with sun, ocean, clouds, rain, river, groundwater.</p>
<p><strong>In a sentence:</strong> "Climate change is intensifying the water cycle, more evaporation, more extreme precipitation, more variability."</p>
