</table>

<h3 id="aquifer">Aquifer</h3>
<p><strong>Definition:</strong> An underground layer of rock or sediment that holds and transmits groundwater. Some are renewable (recharged by rain); some are not.</p>
<p><strong>Visual cue:</strong> Cross-section showing soil + porous rock holding water below the water table.</p>
<p><strong>In a sentence:</strong> "Bangalore's aquifer has been depleting faster than rainfall can recharge it."</p>
