</table>

<h3 id="equity">Equity</h3>
<p><strong>Definition:</strong> Fairness in how benefits + burdens are distributed. Not the same as equality (treating everyone identically); equity accounts for different needs + starting points.</p>
<p><strong>Visual cue:</strong> Three figures of different heights all viewing a fence; equity = providing different boxes to all see over.</p>
<p><strong>In a sentence:</strong> "Climate transition equity means not putting all costs on those least able to bear them."</p>
<table>
  <thead><tr><th>Tamil</th><th>Hindi</th><th>Français</th><th>Korean</th><th>Japanese</th></tr></thead>
  <tbody><tr><td lang="ta">சமத்துவம் / equity</td><td lang="hi">समानता / न्यायसंगता</td><td lang="fr">équité</td><td lang="ko">형평성 / 공평성</td><td lang="ja">公平性・公正性</td></tr></tbody>
</table>

<h3 id="just-transition">Just transition</h3>
<p><strong>Definition:</strong> Energy transition that protects workers + communities affected by the shift away from fossil fuels. Recognizes social costs of change.</p>
<p><strong>Visual cue:</strong> Coal workers transitioning to renewable energy jobs.</p>
<p><strong>In a sentence:</strong> "Cape Town's coal transition requires just-transition strategies for affected mining communities."</p>
